msm-vidc (5.4 msm_vidc on 6.18): control ioctls through the ext-ctrl ops, v4l2_fh_add/del(fh, filp)

- v4l2_ioctl_ops.vidioc_g_ctrl/s_ctrl/queryctrl are gone (v6.18): the core serves
  VIDIOC_G_CTRL/S_CTRL/QUERYCTRL through vidioc_g/s_ext_ctrls and vidioc_query_ext_ctrl.
  New ext ops call vidc's own handlers (msm_vidc_g_ctrl/s_ctrl/query_ctrl) control by
  control, so the 6.12 behaviour (msm_comm_s_ctrl, try_get_ctrl_for_instance, HEVC tier
  stripping, menu_skip_mask flags) is kept. VIDIOC_{G,S}_EXT_CTRLS/QUERY_EXT_CTRL now
  answer instead of -ENOTTY.
- v4l2_fh_add()/v4l2_fh_del() take the struct file (and set/clear filp->private_data):
  msm_vidc_open() only initialises the fh, msm_v4l2_open() adds it (replacing its
  private_data assignment), msm_v4l2_close() deletes it before msm_vidc_close().

